 Minnesota Vikings (\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0116-93510dd7b19c:d07\", \"text\": \"3½ in and 170 pounds ( 77 kg ) , [ 6 ] and was 203 pounds ( 92 kg ) at the end of college . [ 6 ] Lambert was the prototypical middle linebacker for what became the Tampa Two defense . Popularized by the Tampa Bay Buccaneers under Tony Dungy , this defense was originated by Bud Carson , the Steelers defensive coordinator from 1972-1977 . [ 14 ] In Carson 's `` Double-Rotating Zone '' / Cover-2 defense , the safeties played back in a two-deep zone and the cornerbacks played in two shallow zones ,\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"American football\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"Jack Snow was a professional American football player in the NFL during the 1960s. I am certain based on general sports history knowledge.\"}"
